  "evidence": "Original reticle producer/consumer reconstruction.3410 initializes projection origin159/79 separately from neutral reticle160/79. AmigaD35A and alternate2F7xx/3ACxx fold rotation accumulators into signed offsets, add neutral coordinates, store766/768, then clamp separate drawing registers; stored coordinates are not necessarily final clipped sprite coordinates. Weapon spawn copies766/768 to76E/770 before later allocation checks; snapshots do not establish an aim trajectory or reader.73F6 and372F8 choose visible scan candidates using projected extents and depth; selected record pointer6B0, stored type840, even depth846 and projected coordinates7D0/7D2 are shared with identity text, homing missile lock and tractor selection.372F8 preserves registers and has distinct filtering/shift/zero-depth behavior; do not normalize it to73FC. Missile76xx copies selected record into object3C,76D4 refreshes projection; tractor3583C copies candidate to838. No universal object3C field, all-caller validity or lifetime guarantee inferred.34034 decays A74 by300 when stopped/stardrive off and increments100 capped16000 when active in space; projectile speed, projected movement and world-event thresholds consume the same stardrive speed addend. Preserve original signed WORD arithmetic and callback/state assumptions. These facts are static; prior flight/modal evidence does not certify new target-lock or stardrive runtime paths.",
